---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Badge from "../components/Badge.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
import results from "../data/results.json";

const top = [...results.runs].sort((a, b) => b.overall - a.overall).slice(0, 5);
const sampleNote = results._note.includes("SAMPLE DATA");
---
<Base title="The open benchmark for LLMs in public service">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pt-16 pb-12 md:pt-24 md:pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <Badge tone="signal" class="mb-5">Open benchmark · public leaderboard</Badge>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl md:text-6xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight">
        Do language models work<br />for <em class="not-italic text-signal-deep">public service?</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        CivBench measures what government services actually need from AI: correct application
        of policy, plain-language answers, honest uncertainty, and knowing when to hand a case
        to a human. <strong class="text-ink">93 fixtures across 18 categories</strong> — every
        fixture, scorer, and methodology page open for inspection.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/leaderboard" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-ink text-paper font-medium hover:bg-ink-soft">See the leaderboard</a>
        <a href="/founding-argument" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-lg border border-line bg-white font-medium hover:bg-black/5">Why benchmarks fail government</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink-mute">
        The closed alternative keeps its tests secret and sells the scores.
        We publish the tests, the runner, and the scores — and defend against
        contamination in the open. <a href="/contamination" class="underline underline-offset-2">How →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Leaderboard preview -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-8">
    <div class="flex items-end justify-between mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl">Latest scores {sampleNote && <Badge tone="gold" class="ml-2 align-middle">sample data</Badge>}</h2>
      <a href="/leaderboard" class="text-sm text-signal-deep underline underline-offset-2">Full leaderboard →</a>
    </div>
    <Card class="p-0 overflow-hidden">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-line text-left text-ink-mute">
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">#</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Model</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-right">Score</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-right">Cost / task</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {top.map((r, i) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-line last:border-0 hover:bg-paper">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-ink-mute">{i + 1}</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">{r.model} <span class="text-ink-mute font-normal">· {r.vendor}</span></td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-right font-mono">{(r.overall * 100).toFixed(1)}%</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-right font-mono text-ink-mute">${r.cost_per_task_usd?.toFixed(2)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </Card>
    {sampleNote && (
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-ink-mute">Sample rows for site design — the first real eval run will replace them via the runner's JSONL output.</p>
    )}
  </section>

  <!-- Six dimensions -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl mb-2">What standard benchmarks don't measure</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft mb-8 max-w-2xl">Six dimensions where a model can clear every mainstream benchmark and still fail in front of real applicants. Each one is a tested category in CivBench.</p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {[
        ["Policy groundedness", "Cite the rule you applied — or say you can't. Inventing a threshold is worse than abstaining."],
        ["Process correctness", "Right answer via wrong rule-check order still fails. In a regulated process, the procedure is the product."],
        ["Asymmetric error cost", "A false denial isn't a false approval. We tag error direction so scores can be weighted like the real stakes."],
        ["Escalation", "The correct move is often neither 'answer' nor 'refuse' — it's flagging the case for a human, with a reason."],
        ["Plain language", "A determination the applicant can't understand will be appealed or abandoned. We grade readability, not vibes."],
        ["Long-horizon state", "Cases evolve across interviews, life events, recertifications — with reactive counterparties, not single-turn prompts."],
      ].map(([t, d]) => (
        <Card>
          <div class="font-semibold mb-1.5">{t}</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">{d}</p>
        </Card>
      ))}
    </div>
    <a href="/founding-argument" class="inline-block mt-6 text-signal-deep underline underline-offset-2 text-sm">Read the full founding argument →</a>
  </section>

  <!-- Open vs closed -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12">
    <Card class="md:p-10">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div>
          <Badge tone="mint" class="mb-3">CivBench — open</Badge>
          <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-ink-soft">
            <li>✓ Fixtures, scorers, and runner are open source</li>
            <li>✓ Contamination defense published, not whispered about</li>
            <li>✓ Judge-vs-human agreement reported with every judge-graded score</li>
            <li>✓ Anyone can reproduce a run</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <Badge tone="clay" class="mb-3">Closed benchmarks</Badge>
          <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-ink-soft">
            <li>✕ Test materials secret — trust us</li>
            <li>✕ Scores sold to enterprises and agencies</li>
            <li>✕ No way to check what "accuracy" even measured</li>
            <li>✕ $40M of funding deciding what counts</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-mute leading-relaxed">Public-sector AI evaluation shouldn't be a proprietary product. When a model decides — or advises — who gets benefits, the test it passed should be public.</p>
    </Card>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12 text-center">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl mb-3">Run it yourself</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft mb-6 max-w-xl mx-auto">The eval repo has the fixtures, the Inspect AI wiring, and the runner. One command reproduces any score on this page.</p>
    <div class="inline-block text-left bg-ink text-paper rounded-lg px-5 py-4 font-mono text-sm">
      <div><span class="text-ink-mute">$</span> inspect eval src/civbench/inspect_task.py@civbench_deterministic</div>
      <div><span class="text-ink-mute">$</span> python scripts/run_evals.py --model-name my-model --out run.jsonl</div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
